
                          Security Checker v1.01

                 by The Silencer of DoOdLeS^ShoCK^EQUiNøX







If a user logs on your board with a security level over XXX and is not
listed in your config he will be set to a standard harmless security
level of YYY.

For instance if you give a user 255 in security for a Sysop DL or something
and forget to set the securitylevel back, next time that user calls his
sec.level will drop to a harmless level.

This way your board can not be intruded by lamers zooming private mail,
account editing, checking private areas or SysopDL'ing.....


To enable the door to be run EACH time a user logs on you have
to launch it as an MCI command like this in for instance your Bull.txt

---------------------/cut/-------
~
~CC_doorname|
---------------------/cut/-------

..and watch out for supress quick logons etc in your /X setup :)


No stupid configfiles needed just these tooltypes:

   SYSOP_LEVEL = 250            <- Securitylevel to check Sysop.x names
STANDARD_LEVEL = 20             <- Sec.level to be set if user not in Sysop.x
       SYSOP.1 = The Silencer   <- Name of The Sysop's and CoSysop's
       SYSOP.2 = d-Zire         <- that is allowed to have SYSOP_LEVEL



 Small message to Delusion / Virtual - Lame to rip other peoples doors.




